<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">pounce</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">pounce</ansi> command launches a quadruped predator in a
leaping full-body strike that drives the target backward. It
deals heavy damage and has a strong chance to knock the target
to the ground on a successful hit.

<ansi fg="yellow">Requirements:</ansi>

  - Must have legs (leaping requires them)
  - Must have natural fangs or claws (fanged or clawed species)
  - Must be in active combat
  - Cannot be in a grapple (can't leap from a clinch)
  - Cannot be used if special move cooldown is active

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">pounce</ansi>
  Attempt to pounce on your current combat target

<ansi fg="yellow">Mechanics:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="stat">Damage:</ansi> Heavy — the leaping body-slam deals significant
    harm on contact.
  <ansi fg="stat">Knockdown:</ansi> A successful pounce has a strong chance to
    drive the target backward off their feet (Supine),
    leaving them vulnerable to follow-up attacks.
  <ansi fg="stat">Cooldown:</ansi> Shared with other special moves.
  <ansi fg="stat">Skill:</ansi> Progresses Unarmed Combat

Pounce is a powerful opener that combines direct damage with
a knockdown attempt, setting up devastating follow-ups for
sustained predator pressure. See <ansi fg="command">help conditions</ansi> for
details on Supine.

